ministers attending the general affairs  council in brussels on july 23  the first under italian presidency will  discuss the work plan prepared by the  new eu presidency for the next six  months  following the meeting of the european  council on july 16 ministers will also  explore new ways to better monitor the  implementation of decisions taken by eu  leaders  during their meetings in brussels as it  works now  ministers prepare implementation reports  which are then presented to the eu  leaders  but the idea is to make the follow-up  process more effective and less  bureaucratic  ministers will also have a look at the  work that needs to be done until the end  of the year  to prepare the review of the europe 2020  growth strategy  this sets ambitious objectives on  employment innovation  education social inclusion and climate  and energy to be reached by 2020  and as next year's mid-term review of  the strategy approaches  there's a unanimous call to step up  efforts to reach the agreed targets  following the recommendation last month  of the euro area member states  the council is also expected to take the  necessary decisions  to enable lithuania's entry into the  euro club as from the 1st of january  2015.  with lithuania replacing litas for euros  the euro area will soon count  19 member states  you
 

